# This file serves as a reference for sensitive files
# These patterns are already in the main .gitignore

# DO NOT COMMIT:
# - Any .env files with credentials
# - Firebase service account keys (*-firebase-key.json)
# - Google Cloud credentials (*.json with keys)
# - AWS credentials
# - Database backups with user data
# - Any PEM/private keys

# IF YOU ACCIDENTALLY COMMITTED ONE:
# 1. Remove from git history: git rm --cached filename
# 2. Commit: git commit -m "Remove sensitive file"
# 3. Rotate ALL credentials immediately
# 4. Force push if necessary: git push --force
